&lt;p&gt;The separation is clean. Frontend and backend each have their own &lt;code&gt;package.json&lt;/code&gt; and&lt;code&gt;.env.example&lt;/code&gt;, so you can run them independently during development.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Authentication &amp;amp; Security Highlights
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passwords are hashed with bcrypt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JWT tokens protect routes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;OTP email verification via Nodemailer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Role-based access (user vs admin)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Protected routes on both client and server&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Payment Flow
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;User proceeds to checkout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Backend creates a Razorpay order&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frontend opens the Razorpay checkout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;After successful payment, the backend verifies the signature&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Order is created automatically
This is the real integration pattern, not a mock.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Admin Dashboard
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The dashboard shows:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Total users, products, orders, and revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly sales analytics (Recharts)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recent orders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quick management of products, users, and orders
It gives a practical feel of what a real store owner would need day-to-day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




